            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0510" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.1163 Watch Tower/15: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Berlin (Messersmith)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-05-18T17:00:00-04:00">May 18, 1933—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 2, 4 p.m. The Watch Tower Bible and Tract Society greatly appreciated
                    your earlier and successful efforts but now reports that the Governments of
                    Bavaria, Saxony, Thuringia, Lippe, Mecklenburg, Hesse <pb facs="0511" n="407"
                        xml:id="pg407"/> and Wurttemberg, have officially interdicted its activities
                    and confiscated its property valued at about 750,000 Reichsmarks.</p>
                <p>Please investigate, extend appropriate assistance, and telegraph results.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
